QRI’s method is as important as its ontology.

## Method 1 — Divide consciousness into separate proof obligations

QRI explicitly treats consciousness as a set of subproblems rather than one undifferentiated “hard problem.” Its research approach includes philosophy, neuroscience and neurotechnology, with separate attention to state space, structure, valence, binding and other problems.

## Method 2 — Begin with phenomenal invariants

Conventional research often begins:

[
\text{task}
\rightarrow
\text{behaviour}
\rightarrow
\text{neural correlate}.
]

QRI begins:

[
\text{phenomenal regularity}
\rightarrow
\text{mathematical invariant}
